/**
 * Display preferences, kept out of the cartridge on purpose.
 *
 * A cartridge is a game system — its modules, its prompts, its sheet layouts —
 * and its surface is closed. `buildCartridgePayload` emits exactly the keys of
 * the factory payload, the factory payload is *generated by running the legacy
 * build's own factory* (rule 3a), and `tests/golden.test.js` asserts that
 * applying the real 2025 cartridge and rebuilding it reproduces that file key
 * for key. A fiftieth key would fail that test — correctly. The golden fixture
 * is irreplaceable, so the answer is not to change the test; it is that
 * anything which is not part of the legacy cartridge surface does not belong in
 * the cartridge.
 *
 * "Do I want a tracker card under every message" is exactly that: a per-install
 * viewing preference, not a property of the game. It lives here instead — one
 * small file per user, beside `settings.json`, carried by no export.
 *
 * The settings store's own header already anticipated this: *"the saved
 * cartridge library, UI state, connection choices … are settings too, but they
 * are not part of the cartridge surface."* This is the first of them.
 */

